      <!-- 3. USED CAR LOAN SECTION -->
      <h2>Used Car Loan Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Financing a pre-owned vehicle follows similar principles to buying a new vehicle, but lenders often apply customized terms based on the pre-owned vehicle's profile. Using a <strong>used car loan calculator</strong> helps you estimate your monthly commitment based on the vehicle purchase price, upfront down payment, applicable interest rate, loan term, and registration fees.
      </p>
      <p>
        Financing terms and interest rates for used vehicles may differ depending on several key factors:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vehicle Age & Kilometers Driven:</strong> Most lenders restrict the maximum age of the car (often up to 8 to 10 years at loan maturity).</li>
        <li><strong>Vehicle Condition & Valuation:</strong> Certified pre-owned vehicles from authorized dealerships may qualify for better financing terms than private-party sales.</li>
        <li><strong>Lender Policies:</strong> Banks and NBFCs evaluate risk differently for used cars, typically offering loan-to-value (LTV) ratios between 70% and 90%.</li>
        <li><strong>Borrower Eligibility:</strong> Credit scores, income stability, and repayment history influence the sanctioned interest rate.</li>
        <li><strong>Loan Tenure:</strong> Used car tenures are generally shorter (typically 24 to 60 months) compared to new car loans.</li>
      </ul>

