      <!-- 7. CAR LOAN EMI SECTION -->
      <h2>Car Loan EMI Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>car loan calculator emi</strong> uses standard reducing balance mathematics to compute your Equated Monthly Installment. Monthly installment calculations generally depend on three primary variables:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Loan Amount (Principal):</strong> The total amount borrowed after subtracting down payments and trade-in credits from the total purchase price.</li>
        <li><strong>Interest Rate:</strong> The annual percentage rate charged by the financier, converted to a monthly periodic rate (<code>Rate / 12 / 100</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Loan Tenure:</strong> The total number of monthly payments (e.g. 36, 48, 60, or 84 months).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Understanding how an <strong>emi car loan calculator</strong> structures each monthly payment helps you plan your monthly household budget effectively while considering additional vehicle operating costs such as insurance, fuel, and routine maintenance.
