        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. How is a car loan EMI calculated?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Car loan EMIs are calculated using the standard amortizing formula: <code>M = P × [r(1+r)^n] / [(1+r)^n − 1]</code>, where <em>P</em> is the loan principal, <em>r</em> is the monthly interest rate (annual rate / 12 / 100), and <em>n</em> is the total number of monthly payments. If the interest rate is 0%, the monthly payment equals the loan principal divided by the number of months.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
